Design: I propose replacing the standard BCEWithLogitsLoss with a Focal Loss (gamma=2, alpha=0.25) to focus learning on hard and minority-class examples. This change is atomic and integrates seamlessly with the existing mixup and TTA pipelines, aiming to improve AUROC by better handling class imbalance without altering the model architecture or training regimen. The rest of the code, including data loading, augmentation, training loop, and TTA-based evaluation, remains unchanged. We will implement FocalLoss and use it in the mixup loss computation, then train and report the best validation AUROC.
